# Security response headers — kemek-qr
#
# Cloudflare Pages applies this file at deploy time. Each path glob
# attaches the indented headers below it to matching responses.
#
# Locked decision: CSP carries 'unsafe-inline' on script-src and
# style-src. Full rationale, inline-script enumeration (FOUC firewall
# + per-route SvelteKit hydration bootstrap + JSON-LD blocks across
# the page-shell + each landing + about), alternatives considered
# (SHA-256 hash pinning, nonce-based CSP via Pages Function), and
# revisit triggers all live in adrs/0003-csp-unsafe-inline.md (the
# canonical home). Do not relitigate without a real driver.
#
# Other CSP carve-outs (img-src data: blob:, font-src data:,
# connect-src 'self' explicitly excluding cloudflareinsights.com,
# frame-ancestors 'none' + X-Frame-Options DENY) are described in
# the same ADR; their reasoning is brief and lives there to keep
# this file from drifting out of sync with the canonical decision
# record.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=(), magnetometer=(), gyroscope=(), accelerometer=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
